"""The curated rows of the 2022-2026 evidence matrix (Phase II continuation, 12 October 2026).

Every row states only what was read. `evidence` is one of
    FULL_TEXT          every page read
    FULL_TEXT_PARTIAL  the open-access text was read in the sections named in `coverage`; the rest was not
    ABSTRACT           the abstract was read from Crossref, OpenAlex or a repository page; the full text was not (reason in `coverage`)
    TITLE_ONLY         title, authors and venue verified; no abstract could be retrieved
    RETRACTED          the record carries a retraction notice
Fields that the abstract does not state are filled with NR by `build_recent_lit_report.py` (not read), never guessed. Publication facts (venue, volume, pages, online and print dates) come from Crossref
(`recent_core_crossref.csv`) and are joined by DOI; where Crossref has no record the row says so.

relation: SUPPORTS_NEGATIVE (evidence for lower returns after a reliability failure), CHALLENGES_SIGN (positive, null or mechanism-dependent evidence), ADJACENT (different event or outcome, same mechanism family),
DESIGN_STRESS (changes how EXP-014 should be evaluated), PIT_PIPELINE (point-in-time or reproducibility evidence), RETRACTED.
"""

